From bd61ba1e6be445557be268b3b1b963fc3075c027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:47:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mcp: fence the input of channel servers

Give each thread a fence over the input of its channel servers. Closing it
asks every channel server that declares the channel/fence experimental
capability to stop accepting input, emit what it already accepted and then
a marker carrying the fence token. Every initialize carries the current
fence, so a server that restarts or reconnects while it is closed starts
closed, and each connection that becomes ready meanwhile is asked again.
A server without the capability gets no new process, from recovery or
from a new connection, until the fence opens.

The fence reports each channel server's connection, generation, process
and progress, and counts notifications dropped by full queues. Channel
notifications carry the generation of the connection that read them.
